#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the IBM Cloud Resource Controller REST API to get, list, update, and create IBM Quantum Compute Service instances."
msgstr "Use a API REST do IBM Cloud Resource Controller para obter, listar, atualizar e criar instâncias do IBM Quantum Compute Service."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use IBM Cloud Resource Controller API for instance management"
msgstr "Use a API do IBM Cloud Resource Controller para gerenciamento de instâncias"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "{/* cspell:ignore ResourceController  */}\n"
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore Abluemix, apikey */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore ResourceController  */}\n"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use IBM Cloud Resource Controller API for instance management {#use-ibm-cloud-resource-controller-api-for-instance-management}"
msgstr "Use a API do IBM Cloud Resource Controller para gerenciamento de instâncias {#use-ibm-cloud-resource-controller-api-for-instance-management}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can use the IBM Cloud&reg; Resource Controller REST API to programmatically get, create, and update [instances](/guides/instances). \n"
msgstr "Você pode usar a API REST do IBM Cloud&reg; Resource Controller para obter, criar e atualizar [instâncias](/guides/instances) de forma programática. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All Resource Controller endpoints require that you authenticate by passing a header called `Authorization` with the bearer token. Refer to the [REST API setup guide](/guides/cloud-setup-rest-api).\n"
msgstr "Todos os endpoints do Resource Controller exigem que você se autentique passando um cabeçalho chamado `Authorization` com o token bearer. Consulte o [guia de configuração da API REST](/guides/cloud-setup-rest-api).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get an instance {#get-an-instance}"
msgstr "Obter uma instância {#get-an-instance}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the [`GET /v2/resource_instances/{crn}`](https://cloud.ibm.com/apidocs/resource-controller/resource-controller#get-resource-instance) endpoint to get information about a particular instance. The [CRN](/guides/instances) must be URL-encoded in the path.\n"
msgstr "Use o endpoint [`GET /v2/resource_instances/{crn}`](https://cloud.ibm.com/apidocs/resource-controller/resource-controller#get-resource-instance) para obter informações sobre uma instância específica. O [CRN](/guides/instances) deve estar codificado em URL no caminho.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to the standard Resource Controller fields, the response includes quantum-specific fields in both `parameters` and `extensions`. `extensions` stores the instance's normalized metadata, whereas `parameters` only stores the most recent request to modify the instance. Therefore, you should read from `extensions` rather than `parameters`.\n"
msgstr "Além dos campos padrão do Resource Controller, a resposta inclui campos específicos de quantum tanto em `parameters` quanto em `extensions`. `extensions` armazena os metadados normalizados da instância, enquanto `parameters` armazena apenas a solicitação mais recente para modificar a instância. Portanto, você deve ler a partir de `extensions` em vez de `parameters`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `extensions` object includes these fields:\n"
msgstr "O objeto `extensions` inclui estes campos:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`instance_limit_seconds` — Integer, or `null`. The usage time limit for the instance. See [Set instance allocation limits](/guides/allocation-limits).\n"
msgstr "`instance_limit_seconds` — Inteiro, ou `null`. O limite de tempo de uso da instância. Consulte [Definir limites de alocação de instância](/guides/allocation-limits).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`usage_allocation_seconds` — Integer, or `null`. The time allocated to this instance, used by the [fair-share scheduler](/guides/fair-share-scheduler) to determine queue priority. See [Set instance allocation limits](/guides/allocation-limits).\n"
msgstr "`usage_allocation_seconds` — Inteiro, ou `null`. O tempo alocado para esta instância, usado pelo [escalonador de compartilhamento justo](/guides/fair-share-scheduler) para determinar a prioridade na fila. Consulte [Definir limites de alocação de instância](/guides/allocation-limits).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`backends` — Array of strings. The allowlist of backend names available to this instance. `[\"ANY\"]` means all backends on the plan are available (the default). `[]` means no backends are available.\n"
msgstr "`backends` — Array de strings. A lista de permissões dos nomes de backends disponíveis para esta instância. `[\"ANY\"]` significa que todos os backends do plano estão disponíveis (o padrão). `[]` significa que nenhum backend está disponível.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"The backends field may be outdated\">\n"
"  The `backends` field in the `extensions` object may be outdated. This can happen when IBM Quantum Support changes your account in a way that impacts instances. For example, when a backend is removed from an account, it will update the `backends` for the instance, but that change is currently not yet reflected in the Resource Controller API.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"O campo backends pode estar desatualizado\">\n"
"  O campo `backends` no objeto `extensions` pode estar desatualizado. Isso pode acontecer quando o Suporte do IBM Quantum altera sua conta de uma forma que afeta as instâncias. Por exemplo, quando um backend é removido de uma conta, isso atualizará o `backends` da instância, mas essa alteração atualmente ainda não está refletida na API do Resource Controller.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Instead, the current workaround is to use the [IBM Quantum Compute Service REST API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest) with the [`GET /v1/backends`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest/tags/backends#tags__backends__operations__list_backends) endpoint. (Make sure that you set the `Service-CRN` header to your instance's CRN.)\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Em vez disso, a solução alternativa atual é usar a [API REST do IBM Quantum Compute Service](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest) com o endpoint [`GET /v1/backends`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest/tags/backends#tags__backends__operations__list_backends). (Certifique-se de definir o cabeçalho `Service-CRN` com o CRN da sua instância.)\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"curl\" label=\"cURL\">\n"
"    The CRN must be URL-encoded in the path. Replace each `:` with `%3A` and each `/` with `%2F`. For example, `crn:v1:bluemix:...` becomes `crn%3Av1%3Abluemix%3A...`.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"curl\" label=\"cURL\">\n"
"    O CRN deve estar codificado em URL no caminho. Substitua cada `:` por `%3A` e cada `/` por `%2F`. Por exemplo, `crn:v1:bluemix:...` se torna `crn%3Av1%3Abluemix%3A...`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    curl \\\n"
"      --request GET \\\n"
"      --url 'https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN_URL_ENCODED>' \\\n"
"      --header 'Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_BEARER_TOKEN>'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"Python\">\n"
msgstr "  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"Python\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    import urllib.parse\n"
"    import requests\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    crn = \"<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN>\"\n"
"    # We use urllib.parse.quote to URL-encode the CRN.\n"
"    url = (\n"
"        \"https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/\"\n"
"        + urllib.parse.quote(crn, safe=\"\")\n"
"    )\n"
msgstr ""
"    crn = \"<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN>\"\n"
"    # Usamos urllib.parse.quote para codificar o CRN em URL.\n"
"    url = (\n"
"        \"https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/\"\n"
"        + urllib.parse.quote(crn, safe=\"\")\n"
"    )\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    resp = requests.get(\n"
"        url,\n"
"        headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\"},\n"
"        timeout=30,\n"
"    )\n"
"    resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"    print(resp.json())\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    resp = requests.get(\n"
"        url,\n"
"        headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\"},\n"
"        timeout=30,\n"
"    )\n"
"    resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"    print(resp.json())\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get a list of all instances {#get-a-list-of-all-instances}"
msgstr "Obter uma lista de todas as instâncias {#get-a-list-of-all-instances}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the [`GET /v2/resource_instances`](https://cloud.ibm.com/apidocs/resource-controller/resource-controller#list-resource-instances) endpoint to get a list of all your instances. Set the `resource_id` query parameter to `b6049020-80f4-11eb-a0f7-e35ec9b4054f` to filter to IBM Quantum&reg; instances.\n"
msgstr "Use o endpoint [`GET /v2/resource_instances`](https://cloud.ibm.com/apidocs/resource-controller/resource-controller#list-resource-instances) para obter uma lista de todas as suas instâncias. Defina o parâmetro de consulta `resource_id` como `b6049020-80f4-11eb-a0f7-e35ec9b4054f` para filtrar as instâncias do IBM Quantum&reg;.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If your account has multiple plans and you want to filter by plan, set the `resource_plan_id` query parameter to one of the following values:\n"
msgstr "Se sua conta tiver vários planos e você quiser filtrar por plano, defina o parâmetro de consulta `resource_plan_id` como um dos seguintes valores:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Plan | `resource_plan_id` |\n"
"|------|---------------------|\n"
"| Premium | `7f666d17-7893-47d8-bf9d-2b2389fc4dfc` |\n"
"| Flex | `53bde9d3-cdbb-46f5-a98f-60ebcadf7260` |\n"
"| Pay-As-You-Go | `5304b575-3cff-4455-90dc-ae4367762093` |\n"
"| Open | `850b21a7-71de-4e53-9441-1abdd202f35d` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Plano | `resource_plan_id` |\n"
"|------|---------------------|\n"
"| Premium | `7f666d17-7893-47d8-bf9d-2b2389fc4dfc` |\n"
"| Flex | `53bde9d3-cdbb-46f5-a98f-60ebcadf7260` |\n"
"| Pay-As-You-Go | `5304b575-3cff-4455-90dc-ae4367762093` |\n"
"| Open | `850b21a7-71de-4e53-9441-1abdd202f35d` |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each result includes the same `extensions` field as described in [Get an instance](#get-an-instance).\n"
msgstr "Cada resultado inclui o mesmo campo `extensions` descrito em [Obter uma instância](#get-an-instance).\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"curl\" label=\"cURL\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"curl\" label=\"cURL\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    curl \\\n"
"      --request GET \\\n"
"      --url 'https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances?resource_id=b6049020-80f4-11eb-a0f7-e35ec9b4054f' \\\n"
"      --header 'Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_BEARER_TOKEN>'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    import requests\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
